This section contains the procedures and the elements to build special disk images.
Since CP/M 1.4 required a specific sector geometry, the first sectors were ROM compatible to load the Operating System (thus, the monolithic block including BIOS, BDOS and CCP).
When the BIOS is activated, it uses its own disk access routines.

This means that the resulting disk image is hard to edit with disk image editors, it is preferrable to keep the two sections parted.
IMAGEDISK by Dunfield helps to wrap-up the final disk image in the last stage.
